Windows Installation Using a Bootable USB

IT Support Portfolio | Project 01

Overview

This project explains the process of installing Windows using a bootable USB flash drive.

It covers USB preparation, boot menu selection, Windows installation and initial system configuration.

Installation Guide

"Windows Installation Guide" (windows-installation-guide.png)

Requirements

- Computer or laptop
- USB flash drive (8 GB or larger)
- Windows installation media
- Reliable power supply

Installation Steps

1. Prepare the Bootable USB

Create Windows installation media on a USB flash drive using an appropriate installation-media tool.

2. Connect the USB Drive

Insert the bootable USB flash drive into the computer.

3. Access the Boot Menu

Restart the computer and select the USB drive from the boot menu.

4. Start Windows Setup

Choose the preferred language, time format and keyboard layout.

5. Install Windows

Follow the installation instructions and select the correct destination drive.

Important: Back up important files before a clean installation. Selecting the wrong drive may result in data loss.

6. Complete Initial Setup

Allow Windows installation to finish and complete the initial configuration.

Common Installation Problems

- USB drive not detected
- Computer unable to boot from USB
- Storage drive not detected
- Installation interruptions
- Incorrect BIOS/UEFI settings

Expected Result

The computer starts Windows successfully and reaches the desktop, ready for initial configuration.

